Can you help find out the build command?&lt;br/&gt;
I&apos;ve checked that the artifact of 0.7.2 has the same problem.  &lt;br/&gt;
I wonder whether the 2.10 suffix addressed that the artifact should be compile with scala 2.10.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="16076034" author="moon" created="Thu, 6 Jul 2017 06:49:29 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Release artifact in maven repository is created and published by &lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/apache/zeppelin/blob/master/dev/publish_release.sh&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;https://github.com/apache/zeppelin/blob/master/dev/publish_release.sh&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br/&gt;
Do you see some mistake here? \cc &lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=Mina+Lee&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;Mina Lee&quot;&gt;Mina Lee&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="16076417" author="sleefd" created="Thu, 6 Jul 2017 12:16:02 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;var div = new String()&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;In scala 2.10, above sentence in ZeppelinRDisplay.scala should be compiled to&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;ObjectRef div = new ObjectRef(new String());&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;but in scala 2.11, it would be&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;ObjectRef div = ObjectRef.create(new String());&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;I checked the maven deploy command is &lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;mvn clean install -DskipTests  -Pscala-2.10 -Pbeam -Ppublish-distr -Pspark-2.1 -Phadoop-2.6 -Pr -pl !zeppelin-distribution&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;spark-2.1 profile defines the scala version to be 2.11.8 which will override the scala verison in &lt;br/&gt;
 profile scala-2.10, this causes mvn-scala-plugin compiled spark module based on scala 2.11.8.  &lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;scala-2.10 profile doesnt take effects. We should define scalaVersion property evidently in &lt;br/&gt;
maven-scala-plugin for good. Cause mvn-scala-plugin is responsible for scala compiled. &lt;/p&gt;
</comment>
